-- title:
--   Moment bound for the cyclic maximal function
-- statement:
--   For functions $B,C$ on the plane and a kernel $K$, the cyclic kernel output is $\int_{\mathbb R}B(z_2,c)\,C(c,z_1)\,K(z_1+z_2+c)\,dc$, and the hard kernel is $H_{r,R}(t)=\mathbf 1_{r<|t|\le R}/t$. Let $\mathrm{cyclicMax}(B,C)(z)$ be the supremum over rational truncations $0<q_1<q_2$ of $|\mathrm{output}(B,C,H_{q_1,q_2})(z)|$. For $B,C\in L^3(\mathbb R^2)$,
--   $$
--   \int_{\mathbb R^2}\mathrm{cyclicMax}(B,C)(z)^{3/2}\,dz\le C_{\mathrm{mom}}\Bigl(\int|B|^3+\int|C|^3\Bigr).
--   $$
--
--   The bound for finitely many truncations passes to the supremum over all of them.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/TriangularHilbert/CyclicMaxMoment.lean#L58-L71

